      "worked": "Let $f(x)=2e^{x}-x^{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f'(x) &= 2e^{x}-2x\\\\f'(1) &= 2e-2\\\\f(1) &= 2e-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nUse the point-gradient formula with $m_T=2e-2$ and point $(1,2e-1)$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-(2e-1) &= (2e-2)(x-1)\\\\y &= (2e-2)x-(2e-2)+(2e-1)\\\\y &= (2e-2)x+1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
